WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.367
-I'm so happy to see you.
Thank you so much for coming.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.367
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:05.434
Jimmy, are you
my closest friend?

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:06.701
Every time I have
a life milestone,

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.000
I'm coming on "Fallon."

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.133
-Yeah.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.734
-When I got married,
when I was pregnant.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.167
-Last time you were here.

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:14.234
-Yeah, and I gave birth and I
was like, "Okay, call Jimmy.

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:15.934
We've got to get this --"
-Let's get going.

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.000
Yeah, there's another
life moment.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.934
-"I'm going on 'Fallon.'"
-How's baby?

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:21.267
-[ Sighs ]
She's so creamy-dreamy.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:23.167
She's just --
We call her a Twinkie.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:27.133
Just filled with breast milk.
She's chunky.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.901
I'm just -- I'm nibbling.
I'm kissing.

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:29.901
-Yes!

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.334
-You have a baby
to bite the thighs.

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:33.701
-Yes, that's what you do.
That's why people do it.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:35.133
-That's right.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:37.334
You don't get to kiss another
person's baby on the mouth.

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:39.000
That's bizarre.
-Nope.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.033
-And you don't get to bite
other people's baby's thighs.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:43.234
-Yeah, that's correct.
You don't.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:44.300
It's the best.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.934
And I got to see
a picture backstage.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.467
And man, oh, man,
congratulations.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.934
I'm so happy for you.
-Thanks. Thank you.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:52.901
-You -- I also got to see
a photo that you posted

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:55.501
that I think a lot of us can
relate to, a lot of parents.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:57.667
-Yeah.
-This is working right now.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.834
This is you working during
the pandemic.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.868
-Yep, I go from toilet to the --

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.601
-Yeah, exactly.
Yeah. That's you.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.367
-That's my commute from --
-That's your office.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:08.167
-Yeah, from therapy to work,
I'm toilet to edge of tub.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.367
Door is closed most of the time.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:13.701
-Yeah, isn't that inter--
That used to be, like,

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.067
bath is a place for relaxation.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.400
-That's right.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.334
No, now it is work and --
Internal work and external work.

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:20.901
-Yeah. Exactly, yeah.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.167
Are you figuring out
apartment life

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.434
and figuring that all out
with baby?

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.567
-Yeah, being a parent
in New York City is crazy.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.300
I'm just up so many stairs.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.934
I'm like, this is --

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:31.100
As long as I have good form,
it's a workout.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.334
Every day, I'm working out.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:35.000
-You got to make sure your
form is on point.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.000
-I'm tucking the pelvis.
I'm opening the chest.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.400
-Got to work the core.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.634
-Groceries -- I'm like -- I'm
a Sherpa or something.

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.701
I'm just carrying bags.
It's a crazy life.

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:45.734
-You know, you don't think about
this stuff when you're doing it.

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:47.868
-No. I'm like, "Aww, baby."

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:50.434
And then I'm like, groceries
is -- This is bananas.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:51.801
-Yeah.
-This is a trip.

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:55.133
-Yeah. We were talking about --
"Hashtags" earlier was

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:57.133
"MyHighSchoolWasWeird."

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.300
And I was just wondering,
did you have any weird moments

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.968
in high school
or have a weird high school?

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.801
-I mean, like, the weird part --
I went to high school

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.667
on Long Island,
to a big public school,

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:07.868
and I went to school
with like 2,500 kids.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.267
That, to me, was what was weird,

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:13.300
was the feeling
of being cattle, I guess.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.100
We had four minutes.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.434
I think that's
a standard thing --

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:17.801
four minutes between classes.

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:20.033
Running -- Like, it was --

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:22.834
Why can't you get the
fifth minute in high school?

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:25.033
You're already filled
with anxiety and self-loathing

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.901
and just, like,
running past people.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.734
It was just so --
When people talk about

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.434
their high-school experiences
of like,

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:32.834
"Oh, I graduated with
like 20 kids,"

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:33.901
I can't even -- I didn't know --

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:36.534
I knew, you know,
2% of my class.

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:37.734
-That's wild.
-Yeah.

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:39.467
-And were you involved with

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:41.434
any clubs or anything
or teams or --

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:43.067
-I was in student council.
I was a big nerd.

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:46.100
I was in plays
and student council.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.400
And -- ugh! -- I was actually in

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.834
an anti-drug club called
The Positive Edge.

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.267
-Wow.

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:58.934
-I was on the positive edge
of the drug war or something.

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:02.934
And that really worked,
clearly, for me.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.534
Just banking a big part of
my career on weed.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:06.634
-What would happen at
Positive Edge meetings?

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:11.501
-We would talk about --
Honestly, we would cut class.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:12.534
That's what it was.

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:14.501
You did The Positive Edge
to cut class

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:17.767
and go teach fourth and
sixth graders not to do drugs.

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:20.133
And it's lies.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:21.901
It's lies.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.734
We're telling them,
"Don't do drugs, guys,"

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:26.067
as we're starting
to experiment with drugs.

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.100
It was like
the D.A.R.E. program.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.701
Like, did that work?
-Yeah.

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:33.667
-We had, like, a cop come
and tell us how bad drugs were

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:36.734
and some bad guy
is going to sell you drugs.

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:40.067
The truth is that
your friends sell you drugs.

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.400
That's who's pushing it.
-That's interesting.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.367
You're not in
an alleyway somewhere.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.300
-I'm a nerd.
-"Hey, come here a second."

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.067
And it's like it's
your buddies going -- Yeah.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:50.200
-It's my friend stealing
his brother's bong

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.400
and, like, sneaking it like
a dork in his inner pocket.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.567
It's -- No, it didn't work.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:58.400
-Well, you have to kind of
channel your inner high school,

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.934
because "The Afterparty" --
Which, by the way, well done.

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:05.000
-Incredible. So, it was
created by Chris Miller

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.367
and produced by Lord and Miller.

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:09.100
These guys can't miss.
-They really can't.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.801
It's levels of funny and, like,

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:13.267
Easter eggs of fun
and creativity.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:18.033
-Yeah, it was so good.
The cast is bananas.

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:19.167
-Everyone's funny.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:20.567
-It's about
a high-school reunion,

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:22.334
and a pop star
who went to the high school

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:24.667
throws an after party,
played by Dave Franco --

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.234
cracked me up on set.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:30.033
And it becomes
a whodunit murder mystery.

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:34.300
But there's two twists is
